      "created_at": "2025-03-24T17:27:47.252Z",
      "cooked": "<p>There are a few mistakes in your code.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>there just needs to be one or more space between <code>)</code> and <code>{</code>, not the other places.</li>\n<li>in <strong>ERE</strong>, <code>()</code> means a capturing group, to match <code>()</code> literally you need to escape them.</li>\n<li>If you pipe the output of <code>grep</code> to <code>wc -l</code> directly, it will consume the list of files and output only the count. We want to print both, the list and its count. Putting the <code>/dev/tty</code> at the end does not accomplish that.</li>\n<li>Try putting it at a more logical place, where you want to split the incoming <code>stdin</code> into two copies, one to be sent to <code>wc -l</code> to count the lines, and one to the stdout directly to print the lines.</li>\n<li>However, if we redirect to <code>tty</code>, it wont be captured by the <strong>output redirection</strong>. Can you try to fix this?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Also ensure to run <code>synchro init</code> to get the files in your cwd.</p>\n<p>Here’s my solution for your reference:</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler\">\n<pre data-code-wrap=\"bash\"><code class=\"lang-bash\">grep -El \"void main\\(\\)\\s+{$\" *.cpp | tee &gt;(wc -l &gt;&gt; out.txt) &gt; out.txt\n</code></pre>\n</div>",
